    {
      "id": "sort-free-list",
      "name": "SortFreeList",
      "category": "SparseArray",
      "signature": "SortFreeList(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TSparseArray*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Sort the free element list so that subsequent allocations will occur in the lowest available\nposition resulting in tighter packing without moving any existing items. This also means\nthat assigned indices no longer depend on the order in which old items were removed, making\nit easier to use the container when determinism is required (without a container reset).\nE.g., call SortFreeList() each frame to make the container assign the same indices when we\nperform the following operations:\nFrame1: Add(A) -> [0]; Add(B) -> [1]; Remove(A); Remove(B); (Free list is now {[1],[0],...})\nFrame2: Add(A) -> [1]; Add(B) -> [0]; Remove(A); Remove(B); (Free list is now {[0],[1],...})\nNOTE: This is operation is currently O(N) with N = GetMaxIndex(). This could be improved for\nlarge mostly-full arrays if necessary."
    },
